#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046658} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186493997} :activity/id #uuid "ff338657-7250-5578-bcc8-03bd435ba33a" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048893 :topic/id #uuid "c9e24fe5-ad61-5359-b308-a72d2643089c" :topic/math-academy-id 2122} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186493978 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134288 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45044c73-09fa-58fb-ae57-8c07fb707cfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324529} {:answer/id #uuid "667e35b4-0791-5c90-8a77-80282219a6bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324826} {:answer/id #uuid "9dea4603-4170-5303-b0d8-6e693ae1d694" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325310} {:answer/id #uuid "c5916d48-938f-526e-8328-76ddea847a8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325675} {:answer/id #uuid "c747df10-7018-5c0d-8076-0f5bb121d072" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325695}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186325310} :answer-field/id #uuid "172eecd4-ca09-54f5-ab2c-6aae53cb47da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326261}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c185f4ac-1057-5248-8964-7fb26d1dea03" :question/math-academy-id "q-40425" :question/problem "Given the vector $x$ and the system of linear equations below, find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a basis of the solution space of the system. \n\nConsider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system, which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is $1$ pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we get ${x}_{1}=-{x}_{2}.$ So, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\}$ is a basis of the solution space of the system.\n\nFinally, we find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{11\\cdot (-1)+3\\cdot 1}{{(-1)}^{2}+{1}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{-8}{2}b \\\\  & =-4b \\\\  & =-4[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "0a7c3978-56f8-5be3-997f-dd9a4f1bdf46" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494066}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186493991 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186417869 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00506e35-c298-5a4f-af8f-eeaca76aaacb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417839} {:answer/id #uuid "00f093fe-bc06-5628-b62a-e67a521941bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417841} {:answer/id #uuid "6e7a673d-e4a8-5264-a60e-b71b9cc758bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-10 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417853} {:answer/id #uuid "7e7fd9d7-1875-5e28-9d53-6079344fc1c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417857} {:answer/id #uuid "d4d3edfc-faf6-56f0-8a2f-d23798f45713" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417861}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186417853} :answer-field/id #uuid "389ac663-f6cc-5412-8d70-af0f32538d7c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417865}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "169ca18b-315b-5001-b32b-2f9efd14b654" :question/math-academy-id "q-86755" :question/problem "Given the vector $x$ and the system of linear equations below, find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a basis of the solution space of the system. \n\nConsider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system, which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there are $2$ pivot columns ($1$st and $2$nd). Thus, ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. Now, from the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=2{x}_{3}.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-3\\cdot (2{x}_{3})+{x}_{3}=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=5{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{3} \\\\ 2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\}$ is a basis of the solution space of the system.\n\nFinally, we find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{(-9)\\cdot 5+(-5)\\cdot 2+(-5)\\cdot 1}{{5}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{-60\\,}{\\,\\,\\,30\\,}b \\\\  & =-2b \\\\  & =-2[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-10 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "33038e04-8255-5530-ac72-35d4ad10ba81"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186493997 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186417871 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1eea3622-1f9b-5d11-8dea-d8c47cf376cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "z=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417843} {:answer/id #uuid "2667df2c-9f3d-591c-b400-004bf838a4aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "z=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417844} {:answer/id #uuid "7876d49c-79f4-5357-89f7-c467fcc3fef7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "z=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417856} {:answer/id #uuid "9045d64a-6a59-57ea-bac4-733ec53b1337" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "z=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417858} {:answer/id #uuid "c8161b4f-175c-56ad-8c8c-3bb5a54a6cf2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "z=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417860}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186417860} :answer-field/id #uuid "5bd6575e-57c0-5c94-ab1b-632324adbb58" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417866}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3365c089-bf35-5299-ad47-d460e03b5d34" :question/math-academy-id "q-40381" :question/problem "Let $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $a=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ If $x=y+z,$ where $y\\in \\text{Span}\\{a\\}$ and $z⊥\\text{Span}\\{a\\},$ then $z=$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/d8/d887852fe51f08cb7296437e69b6a9632721cfd155558e6abf9a99b4f59f7ad6.png)\n\nFirst, we find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}\\{a\\}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,x & =\\frac{a\\cdot x}{a\\cdot a}a \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 3+3\\cdot 7+(-3)(-6)+1\\cdot 1}{{2}^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{1}^{2}}a \\\\  & =\\frac{6+21+18+1}{4+9+9+1}a \\\\  & =\\frac{46}{23}a \\\\  & =2a \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ z & =x-{\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $y\\in \\text{Span}\\{a\\}$ and $z⊥\\text{Span}\\{a\\},$ as shown in the picture above.\n\nIn conclusion, $z=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$"} :step/id #uuid "42d6a83e-c70e-50e5-a15f-f59fe7b2b27f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494041}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494041 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326840 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16a1e738-b3ef-5617-b65b-5d1f78a95729" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324172} {:answer/id #uuid "89c9f2ab-6dfa-5033-9188-0d8f7909b792" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325144} {:answer/id #uuid "a070fc81-cb3f-5111-b4d2-2fc2ca2fcb13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325332} {:answer/id #uuid "b26dd048-2cb5-50ad-b8cc-18bbc89f309d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325500} {:answer/id #uuid "c8339040-d0af-5ec3-87ec-5da28e3ea2d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325706}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186325332} :answer-field/id #uuid "db70c3b6-c34e-5eef-8233-7d0b5498da99" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326618}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "334df9d1-dd1e-5b54-85c8-f150ef338d78" :question/math-academy-id "q-40411" :question/problem "Let $x=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the distance between $x$ and $\\text{Span}\\{b\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "The distance between the vector $x$ and the vector space $\\text{Span}\\{b\\}$ is given by $‖x-\\overset{^}{x}‖$, where $\\overset{^}{x}$ in the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto $\\text{span}\\{b\\}.$\n\nFirst, we find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}\\{b\\}.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,x & =\\frac{b\\cdot x}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot (-2)+(-1)\\cdot 2+1\\cdot (-2)+(-1)(-2)}{(1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{-2-2-2+2}{1+1+1+1}b \\\\  & =-b \\\\  & =-1[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=\\overset{^}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖x-\\overset{^}{x}‖ & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{3})^{2}+({x}_{4}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{4})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{((-2)-(-1))^{2}+(2-1)^{2}+((-2)-(-1))^{2}+((-2)-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1+1+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{12} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "9b0f69b0-253f-59a9-ae75-3ab70a053b30" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186493978}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494066 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186394140 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07520d50-a4df-570f-97df-ea8a8feaea26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394142} {:answer/id #uuid "5157b3e4-abda-5d47-825b-73f4874a84d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394143} {:answer/id #uuid "c50f8fd6-54a4-564a-a2c4-1085a4288860" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-12 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394144} {:answer/id #uuid "0dacbed5-e0ce-50a6-87c6-1cd849329c37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394145} {:answer/id #uuid "c344c455-0d20-5551-bd65-820a29119155" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394146}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186394145} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e0e70c3-1109-58cb-a447-88acb9d0e5b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394141}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "8bc5c35e-337a-5a6f-8888-1b0686935cc0" :question/math-academy-id "q-81200" :question/problem "Given the vector $x$ and the system of linear equations below, find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}-8{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a basis of the solution space of the system. \n\nConsider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system, which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -5 & -8 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -8 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there are $2$ pivot columns ($1$st and $2$nd). Thus, ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. Now, from the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=2{x}_{3}.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-3\\cdot (2{x}_{3})=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=6{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}6{x}_{3} \\\\ 2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\}$ is a basis of the solution space of the system.\n\nFinally, we find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\cdot 6+5\\cdot 2+0\\cdot 1}{{6}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{82}{41}b \\\\  & =2b \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "ed883a17-ffee-595d-8044-92cfccdf6e88" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186493991}}] :activity/title "Projecting Vectors Onto One-Dimensional Subspaces" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493390}]}
